       "id": "1a.1",
       "text": "The Ashfell Slide affected the mining region around Dreth from March 14, 2026, involving the Withel terraces, Cranmoor and the Ashfell bench.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      },
      {
       "id": "1a.2",
       "text": "A failure of the Ashfell bench damaged the lower road and disrupted service at the Corvane mine, with attribution to mining activity contested.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      },
      {
       "id": "1a.3",
       "text": "Human impact was reported as evacuation and displacement, with about 60 households leaving the Withel terraces and 60 households moving away from Cranmoor.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      },
      {
       "id": "1a.4",
       "text": "Warnings and evacuations were issued for the affected settlements, the lower road was restored, and Yelverton Minerals and an independent panel revised policy.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      }
     ]
    }
